{"correlation_id": "cc0ef81a-dee7-4f5a-8378-734043b8e4b6", "event": "final_received", "final": {"answer": "The purpose of a move-in inspection checklist is to document the condition of a rental property at the start of a tenancy, protect both tenants and landlords by providing a clear record, and facilitate a fair comparison at the end of the tenancy.", "correlation_id": "cc0ef81a-dee7-4f5a-8378-734043b8e4b6", "draft": "A move-in inspection checklist documents the initial condition of a rental property, protects both tenants and landlords by providing a clear record, and facilitates a fair comparison at the end of the tenancy.", "from_stage": "reviewer", "input_source": {"offset": 14, "partition": 0, "topic": "s6102_drafts"}, "plan": "A move-in inspection checklist serves to document the condition of a rental property at the start of a tenancy. Here are three short steps:\n\n1. **Document Initial Condition**: List all aspects of the property, such as walls, floors, appliances, and fixtures, noting any existing damage or wear.\n2. **Protect Tenants and Landlords**: Provide a clear record for both tenants and landlords regarding the property's state, helping to avoid disputes over repairs or maintenance at the end of the tenancy.\n3. **Facilitate Move-Out Inspection**: Use the initial checklist as a basis for comparing conditions at the end of the tenancy, ensuring a fair assessment of any necessary repairs or cleaning.", "question": "Explain the purpose of a move-in inspection checklist.", "rental_context": {"data_version": 12, "dataset_id": "0e586d72da6211f1ae011ab4cc3919df", "listings": [], "requested_codes": []}, "run_id": "question-cc0ef81a-dee7-4f5a-8378-734043b8e4b6", "status": "approved", "writer_instance": "writer-7100"}, "offset": 14, "partition": 0, "pid": 7197, "run_id": "question-cc0ef81a-dee7-4f5a-8378-734043b8e4b6", "source_commit": "52c8ef470b124605a0fc51dd8c5821b4a5f3738b", "student": "Pragya Apurva", "timestamp": "2026-11-07T04:21:25.632684+00:00", "topic": "s6102_final"}
